   "page": 1,
   "source": "layout-regroup",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "text": "This variety arose from the controlled pollination of the\nvariety ‘Norgleam’ by the pollen parent ‘Coliban’. It was\nbred by Dr Roger Kirkham of Healesville, Victoria between\n1980 and 1991. ‘Wilwash’ was selected for its superior\nyield, smooth white-skinned tubers of uniform size, shape\nand cooking qualities fram 20,000 field grown plants.",
